<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Ablation Study on Validation Layers</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We investigated the impact of the validation layer’s depth on generation quality under a fixed <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> speed-up setting. Our results, summarized in Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ C.1. Ablation Study on Validation Layers ‣ Appendix C Trajectory Analysis ‣ SpeCa: Accelerating Diffusion Transformers with Speculative Feature Caching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, indicate that validating at deeper layers consistently improves performance. This finding supports our analysis that deeper layers, which accumulate more prediction errors throughout the denoising process, serve as more reliable indicators of the final output’s fidelity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Further evidence is presented in Section 4.5, where we show that the final layer (Layer 27) exhibits the strongest correlation (<math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.842" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.842</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.842</annotation></semantics></math>) with the image-level reconstruction error. This significantly outperforms both shallow layers (Layer 0: <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.582" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.582</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.582</annotation></semantics></math>) and middle layers (Layer 18: <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.637" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.637</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.637</annotation></semantics></math>). Consequently, these results justify our choice to use features from deep layers for efficient and accurate verification.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6. </span><span id="A3.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation of the Verify layer in DiT at <math id="A3.T6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> speed.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A3.T6.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T6.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><span id="A3.T6.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Method</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><span id="A3.T6.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">FID<span id="A3.T6.4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A3.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><span id="A3.T6.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">sFID<span id="A3.T6.4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A3.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></td>
