<td id="A5.T8.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><math id="A5.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm</td>
<td id="A5.T8.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;">18.88</td>
<td id="A5.T8.4.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;">0.912</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T8.4.6" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="A5.T8.4.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><math id="A5.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.T8.4.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">-norm</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.4.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><span id="A5.T8.4.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">19.28</span></td>
<td id="A5.T8.4.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;"><span id="A5.T8.4.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">0.984</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1. </span>Relationship to Noise Schedules</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A key advantage of SpeCa is its independence from the noise schedule’s functional form. Unlike traditional acceleration methods often tailored to specific schedules (e.g., linear or cosine), SpeCa operates by evaluating predictive consistency directly in the latent feature space. This decouples the acceleration from the analytical properties of the noise progression.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, SpeCa employs a dynamic step-sizing mechanism, contrasting with the fixed or predetermined steps in methods like DDIM and DPM-Solver. It adaptively adjusts step sizes based on the local smoothness of the feature manifold and the reliability of predictions. This inherent flexibility allows SpeCa to be applied across models with diverse noise schedules without requiring re-tuning or prior knowledge of the noise mechanism, making it a more general and broadly applicable acceleration framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Anonymous Page for Video Presentation</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further showcase the advantages of <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span> in video generation, we have created an anonymous GitHub page. For a more detailed demonstration, please visit <a href="https://speca2025.github.io/SpeCa2025/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://speca2025.github.io/SpeCa2025/</a>. Additionally, the videos are also available in the Supplementary Material.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1. </span>Error Propagation Analysis</h3>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem G.1 (Prediction Error Bound).</h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For an <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th order Taylor expansion predictor with sampling interval <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, the prediction error at step <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e_{k}\|_{2}\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{k^{m+2}}{(m+2)!N^{m+2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e_{k}\|_{2}\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{k^{m+2}}{(m+2)!N^{m+2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the Lipschitz constant of the feature evolution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Taylor expansion of <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{m}\frac{(-k)^{i}}{i!N^{i}}\Delta^{i}\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})+R_{m}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{m}\frac{(-k)^{i}}{i!N^{i}}\Delta^{i}\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})+R_{m}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where }R_{m}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where }R_{m}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(-k)^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\mathcal{F}^{(m+1)}(\xi),\ \xi\in[t-k,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(-k)^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\mathcal{F}^{(m+1)}(\xi),\ \xi\in[t-k,t]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For diffusion models, the feature evolution is governed by the underlying stochastic differential equation:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l})=\mu(\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l}),\tau)d\tau+\sigma(\tau)dW_{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l})=\mu(\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l}),\tau)d\tau+\sigma(\tau)dW_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is the drift term, <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the diffusion coefficient, and <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Wiener process.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Due to the smoothness properties of the diffusion process, we can bound the higher-order derivatives. Let <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th derivative of the feature with respect to time. For the drift and diffusion coefficients in diffusion models, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu(\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l}),\tau)\|_{2}\leq L\|\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu(\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l}),\tau)\|_{2}\leq L\|\mathcal{F}(x_{\tau}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the Lipschitz constant of the drift term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the theory of finite differences, the approximation error of the finite difference operator is bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta^{i}\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})-N^{i}\mathcal{F}^{(i)}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\leq CN^{i+1}\|\mathcal{F}^{(i+1)}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta^{i}\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})-N^{i}\mathcal{F}^{(i)}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\leq CN^{i+1}\|\mathcal{F}^{(i+1)}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some constant <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, under the Lipschitz continuity assumption, we can establish:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta^{i}\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\leq(2L)^{i}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta^{i}\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\leq(2L)^{i}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This bound follows from the recursive application of the Lipschitz property across successive timesteps. For the <math id="A7.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th derivative, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}^{(i)}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\leq L^{i}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}^{(i)}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\leq L^{i}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying these bounds to the remainder term:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|R_{m}(k)\|_{2}\leq\frac{k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}L^{m+1}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|R_{m}(k)\|_{2}\leq\frac{k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}L^{m+1}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The prediction error is thus:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\|\mathcal{F}_{\text{pred}}(x_{t-k}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}&amp;=\|R_{m}(k)\|_{2}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\\
&amp;+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{k^{m+2}}{(m+2)!N^{m+2}}\right)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\|\mathcal{F}_{\text{pred}}(x_{t-k}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}&amp;=\|R_{m}(k)\|_{2}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}\\
&amp;+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{k^{m+2}}{(m+2)!N^{m+2}}\right)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The relative error is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\|\mathcal{F}_{\text{pred}}(x_{t-k}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}}{\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\|\mathcal{F}_{\text{pred}}(x_{t-k}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}}{\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">To relate <math id="A7.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the reverse Lipschitz condition:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}\geq(1-\frac{Lk}{N})\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t-k}^{l})\|_{2}\geq(1-\frac{Lk}{N})\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">which follows from the fact that the feature evolution in diffusion models exhibits controlled decay properties.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this lower bound:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\frac{\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}}{(1-\frac{Lk}{N})\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}}+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\frac{\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}}{(1-\frac{Lk}{N})\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}}+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\frac{1}{1-\frac{Lk}{N}}+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\frac{1}{1-\frac{Lk}{N}}+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For small values of <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{Lk}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{Lk}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is typically the case in our setting), we can approximate <math id="A7.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\frac{Lk}{N}}\approx 1+\frac{Lk}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\frac{Lk}{N}}\approx 1+\frac{Lk}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\left(1+\frac{Lk}{N}\right)+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}\left(1+\frac{Lk}{N}\right)+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}+\frac{L^{m+2}k^{m+2}}{(m+1)!N^{m+2}}+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}+\frac{L^{m+2}k^{m+2}}{(m+1)!N^{m+2}}+\mathcal{O}(k^{m+2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{k^{m+2}}{N^{m+2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{L^{m+1}k^{m+1}}{(m+1)!N^{m+1}}+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{k^{m+2}}{N^{m+2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof of the error bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2. </span>Convergence Guarantee</h3>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem G.2 (Distributional Convergence).</h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When the verification threshold schedule satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}=\tau_{0}\cdot\beta^{\frac{T-t}{T}}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}=\tau_{0}\cdot\beta^{\frac{T-t}{T}}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the generated distribution <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{Spec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Spec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{Spec}}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{orig}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">orig</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{orig}}</annotation></semantics></math> in total variation distance:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to\infty}\|p_{\text{Spec}}-p_{\text{orig}}\|_{\text{TV}}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Spec</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">orig</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to\infty}\|p_{\text{Spec}}-p_{\text{orig}}\|_{\text{TV}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We decompose the proof into three main components: first establishing the relationship between feature errors and output image errors, then analyzing the error propagation through the diffusion process, and finally proving convergence in the distribution space.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1. Noise Schedule Compatibility:<span id="A7.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In diffusion models, the denoising process at timestep <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(x_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\right)+\sigma_{t}z" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(x_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\right)+\sigma_{t}z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> is the random noise added during sampling, and <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=\sqrt{\beta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=\sqrt{\beta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the output generated using the original model and <math id="A7.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the output from our </span><span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span><span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text"> framework. The error between these outputs can be expressed as:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\|x_{t-1}-x_{t-1}^{*}\|_{2}&amp;=\left\|\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(x_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\right)\right.\\
&amp;\quad\left.-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(x_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tau_{\theta}^{*}(x_{t},t)\right)\right\|_{2}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\|\tau_{\theta}^{*}(x_{t},t)-\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\|_{2}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\|x_{t-1}-x_{t-1}^{*}\|_{2}&amp;=\left\|\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(x_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\right)\right.\\
&amp;\quad\left.-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(x_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tau_{\theta}^{*}(x_{t},t)\right)\right\|_{2}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\|\tau_{\theta}^{*}(x_{t},t)-\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\|_{2}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The predicted noise <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of the feature representation <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the Lipschitz continuity of the mapping from features to noise predictions, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tau_{\theta}^{*}(x_{t},t)-\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\|_{2}\leq K\|\mathcal{F}^{*}(x_{t}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tau_{\theta}^{*}(x_{t},t)-\tau_{\theta}(x_{t},t)\|_{2}\leq K\|\mathcal{F}^{*}(x_{t}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the Lipschitz constant of the mapping.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting our definition of relative error <math id="A7.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}^{*}(x_{t}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}=e_{t}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}^{*}(x_{t}^{l})-\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}=e_{t}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(33)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{t-1}-x_{t-1}^{*}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{t-1}-x_{t-1}^{*}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}K\cdot e_{t}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}K\cdot e_{t}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(34)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{t}\cdot e_{t}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{t}\cdot e_{t}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}K</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our verification condition ensures:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(35)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{t}\leq\tau_{t}=\tau_{0}\cdot\beta^{\frac{T-t}{T}}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{t}\leq\tau_{t}=\tau_{0}\cdot\beta^{\frac{T-t}{T}}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|x_{t-1}-x_{t-1}^{*}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|x_{t-1}-x_{t-1}^{*}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{t}\cdot\sqrt{\frac{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{t}\cdot\sqrt{\frac{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}\cdot(\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}+\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(37)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx C_{t}\cdot\sqrt{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}\cdot\frac{\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}}{\sqrt{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx C_{t}\cdot\sqrt{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}\cdot\frac{\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}}{\sqrt{1+\|\mathcal{F}(x_{t}^{l})\|_{2}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(38)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{t}\cdot\sqrt{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{t}\cdot\sqrt{\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">This bounds the per-step error in terms of the diffusion noise schedule.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2. Martingale Analysis:<span id="A7.SS2.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now analyze the error accumulation across multiple steps. Define the error process:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(39)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}=\|x_{t}-x_{t}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}-\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}=\|x_{t}-x_{t}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}-\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}=x_{s}-\mathbb{E}[x_{s}|x_{s+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}=x_{s}-\mathbb{E}[x_{s}|x_{s+1}]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the error introduced at step <math id="A7.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can show that <math id="A7.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a martingale with respect to the filtration <math id="A7.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (the information available up to time <math id="A7.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(40)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{t+1}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[M_{t+1}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|x_{t+1}-x_{t+1}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]-\sum_{s=1}^{t+1}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|x_{t+1}-x_{t+1}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]-\sum_{s=1}^{t+1}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(41)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|x_{t}-x_{t}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|x_{t}-x_{t}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(42)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]-\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]-\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(43)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=M_{t}+\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]-\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=M_{t}+\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]-\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under our verification threshold condition, the error <math id="A7.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded such that:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(45)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(46)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[M_{t+1}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]=M_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[M_{t+1}|\mathcal{F}_{t}]=M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">This confirms that <math id="A7.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed a martingale.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the martingale to converge, we need to verify the Lindeberg condition:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(47)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t}\|_{2}^{4}]}{\beta_{t}^{2}}&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t}\|_{2}^{4}]}{\beta_{t}^{2}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under our threshold schedule, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(48)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t}\|_{2}^{4}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t}\|_{2}^{4}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{t}^{4}\cdot(\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{t}^{4}\cdot(\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(49)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{K^{4}(1-\alpha_{t})^{4}}{\alpha_{t}^{2}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})^{2}}\cdot(\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{K^{4}(1-\alpha_{t})^{4}}{\alpha_{t}^{2}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})^{2}}\cdot(\beta_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(50)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=K^{4}\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})^{4}\beta_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=K^{4}\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})^{4}\beta_{t}^{2}}{\alpha_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(51)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t}\|_{2}^{4}]}{\beta_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{t}\|_{2}^{4}]}{\beta_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}K^{4}\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})^{4}}{\alpha_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}K^{4}\frac{(1-\alpha_{t})^{4}}{\alpha_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">In diffusion models, the schedule typically satisfies <math id="A7.SS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A7.SS2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to T</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring the above sum is finite.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the martingale convergence theorem, <math id="A7.SS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> converges almost surely, implying:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(53)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to T}\left(\|x_{t}-x_{t}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}-\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]\right)=M_{\infty}&lt;\infty\text{ a.s.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> a.s.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to T}\left(\|x_{t}-x_{t}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}-\sum_{s=1}^{t}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]\right)=M_{\infty}&lt;\infty\text{ a.s.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3. Convergence in Distribution:<span id="A7.SS2.p22.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we need to translate the almost sure convergence of the error process to convergence in distribution. For diffusion models, the total variation distance between the generated distributions can be bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(54)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{\text{Spec}}-p_{\text{orig}}\|_{\text{TV}}\leq\mathbb{E}[\|x_{0}-x_{0}^{*}\|_{2}]\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[\|x_{0}-x_{0}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>Spec</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>orig</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{\text{Spec}}-p_{\text{orig}}\|_{\text{TV}}\leq\mathbb{E}[\|x_{0}-x_{0}^{*}\|_{2}]\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[\|x_{0}-x_{0}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">From our martingale analysis:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(55)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|x_{0}-x_{0}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[M_{0}]+\sum_{s=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[M_{T}]+\sum_{s=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|x_{0}-x_{0}^{*}\|_{2}^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[M_{0}]+\sum_{s=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[M_{T}]+\sum_{s=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under our threshold schedule, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(56)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]\leq\sum_{s=1}^{T}C_{s}^{2}\cdot\beta_{s}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{s})\to 0\text{ as }T\to\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\tau_{s}\|_{2}^{2}]\leq\sum_{s=1}^{T}C_{s}^{2}\cdot\beta_{s}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{s})\to 0\text{ as }T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(57)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to\infty}\|p_{\text{Spec}}-p_{\text{orig}}\|_{\text{TV}}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>Spec</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>orig</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext>TV</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to\infty}\|p_{\text{Spec}}-p_{\text{orig}}\|_{\text{TV}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof of distributional convergence.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3. </span>Computational Complexity</h3>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem G.3 (Speedup Lower Bound).</h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With acceptance rate <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and verification cost ratio <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the speedup ratio <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(58)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\geq\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma-\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">overhead</mtext></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\geq\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma-\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{overhead}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">overhead</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the constant-time overhead.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish a comprehensive understanding of the computational complexity, we analyze the component-wise breakdown of both the traditional diffusion sampling and our </span><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span><span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text"> approach.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1. Traditional Diffusion Sampling:<span id="A7.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The standard diffusion model inference requires <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> sequential denoising steps, each requiring a full forward pass through the model. Let <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> denote the computational cost of a single forward pass. The total computational complexity is:</span></span></p>
<table id="A7.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(59)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{standard}}=T\cdot C" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>standard</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{standard}}=T\cdot C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2. <span id="A7.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span> Computational Components:<span id="A7.SS3.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us break down the computation in </span><span id="A7.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span><span id="A7.SS3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text">:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(a) Full computation steps: These are the steps where we perform a complete forward pass through the diffusion model. If we denote the number of such steps as <math id="A7.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{full}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{full}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the computational cost is:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(60)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{full}}\cdot C" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{full}}\cdot C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(b) Prediction steps: For the speculative steps, we use TaylorSeer to predict features for subsequent timesteps. The computational cost of prediction is negligible compared to a full forward pass, but we include it for completeness:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(61)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{spec}}\cdot C_{\text{pred}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{spec}}\cdot C_{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{pred}}\ll C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo>≪</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{pred}}\ll C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(c) Verification steps: For each speculative prediction, we need to validate its accuracy using our lightweight verification mechanism. This involves computing the relative error between the predicted features and the actual features. The cost per verification is:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(62)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{verify}}=\gamma\cdot C+C_{\text{overhead}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>verify</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{verify}}=\gamma\cdot C+C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the ratio of the verification cost to the full forward pass cost, and <math id="A7.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{overhead}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant overhead independent of the model size.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">In modern diffusion architectures (DiT, FLUX, HunyuanVideo), the verification only requires comparing features in the final layer, resulting in <math id="A7.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Our empirical measurements show <math id="A7.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\approx 0.035" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.035</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\approx 0.035</annotation></semantics></math> for DiT, <math id="A7.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\approx 0.0175" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.0175</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\approx 0.0175</annotation></semantics></math> for FLUX, and <math id="A7.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\approx 0.0167" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.0167</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\approx 0.0167</annotation></semantics></math> for HunyuanVideo.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3. Total Computation for <span id="A7.SS3.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span>:<span id="A7.SS3.p9.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The total computational cost for </span><span id="A7.SS3.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span><span id="A7.SS3.p10.1.3" class="ltx_text"> is:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(63)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T_{\text{full}}\cdot C+T_{\text{spec}}\cdot C_{\text{pred}}+T_{\text{spec}}\cdot C_{\text{verify}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>verify</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T_{\text{full}}\cdot C+T_{\text{spec}}\cdot C_{\text{pred}}+T_{\text{spec}}\cdot C_{\text{verify}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(64)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx T_{\text{full}}\cdot C+T_{\text{spec}}\cdot(\gamma\cdot C+C_{\text{overhead}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx T_{\text{full}}\cdot C+T_{\text{spec}}\cdot(\gamma\cdot C+C_{\text{overhead}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we have neglected <math id="A7.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{pred}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math> as it is significantly smaller than other terms.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4. Acceptance Rate Analysis:<span id="A7.SS3.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the acceptance rate <math id="A7.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as the ratio of speculative steps to total steps:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(65)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\frac{T_{\text{spec}}}{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\frac{T_{\text{spec}}}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">This means <math id="A7.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{full}}=T-T_{\text{spec}}=T(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>full</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>spec</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{full}}=T-T_{\text{spec}}=T(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting into our total computation formula:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(66)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T(1-\alpha)\cdot C+T\alpha\cdot(\gamma\cdot C+C_{\text{overhead}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T(1-\alpha)\cdot C+T\alpha\cdot(\gamma\cdot C+C_{\text{overhead}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(67)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=TC(1-\alpha)+T\alpha\gamma C+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=TC(1-\alpha)+T\alpha\gamma C+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(68)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=TC[1-\alpha+\alpha\gamma]+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=TC[1-\alpha+\alpha\gamma]+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(69)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=TC[1-\alpha(1-\gamma)]+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=TC[1-\alpha(1-\gamma)]+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5. Speedup Ratio:<span id="A7.SS3.p14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">The speedup ratio <math id="A7.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the ratio of the standard computation time to the </span><span id="A7.SS3.p15.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span><span id="A7.SS3.p15.1.3" class="ltx_text"> computation time:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(70)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{T_{\text{standard}}}{T_{\text{total}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>standard</mtext></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{T_{\text{standard}}}{T_{\text{total}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(71)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{TC}{TC[1-\alpha(1-\gamma)]+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{TC}{TC[1-\alpha(1-\gamma)]+T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(72)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma)+\frac{T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}}{TC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma)+\frac{T\alpha C_{\text{overhead}}}{TC}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(73)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma)+\alpha\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma)+\alpha\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(74)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha+\alpha\gamma+\alpha\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha+\alpha\gamma+\alpha\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(75)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma-\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma-\frac{C_{\text{overhead}}}{C})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6. Practical Approximation:<span id="A7.SS3.p16.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">For modern architectures where <math id="A7.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\gg C_{\text{overhead}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≫</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>overhead</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\gg C_{\text{overhead}}</annotation></semantics></math> (the model computation dominates over any constant overhead), and with <math id="A7.SS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\approx 0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\approx 0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, we can approximate:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(76)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{1-\alpha(1-\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(77)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{1-\alpha(0.95)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{1-\alpha(0.95)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(78)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{1-0.95\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.95</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{1-0.95\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A7.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> approaches 1 (high acceptance rate), the speedup approaches <math id="A7.SS3.p18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{0.05}=20\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>0.05</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{0.05}=20\times</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, we observe acceptance rates of approximately <math id="A7.SS3.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.85</annotation></semantics></math> across various models and datasets, resulting in speedups around <math id="A7.SS3.p18.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{1-0.95\cdot 0.85}\approx\frac{1}{0.1925}\approx 5.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.95</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>0.1925</mn></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>5.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-0.95\cdot 0.85}\approx\frac{1}{0.1925}\approx 5.2\times</annotation></semantics></math>, which aligns with our experimental results.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">This analysis demonstrates that </span><span id="A7.SS3.p19.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SpeCa</span><span id="A7.SS3.p19.1.3" class="ltx_text">’s efficiency directly correlates with the acceptance rate of speculative predictions, with theoretical maximum speedups approaching <math id="A7.SS3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A7.SS3.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.3.1. </span>Adaptive Threshold Selection</h4>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The adaptive threshold is a critical component in balancing the trade-off between acceleration and quality. We adopt a timestep-dependent threshold schedule:</p>
<table id="A7.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(79)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}=\tau_{0}\cdot\beta^{\frac{T-t}{T}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}=\tau_{0}\cdot\beta^{\frac{T-t}{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial threshold, <math id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the decay factor, and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of timesteps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This schedule is motivated by the following observations:</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">1. <span id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Noise Level Correlation</span>: In early timesteps (large <math id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>), the diffusion process is dominated by random noise, making feature predictions more reliable and allowing for higher thresholds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">2. <span id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detail Sensitivity</span>: As <math id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> decreases, the diffusion process focuses on generating fine details, requiring stricter thresholds to maintain visual quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">3. <span id="A7.SS3.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error Propagation</span>: Errors in early timesteps have greater impact on final quality due to error accumulation, necessitating an exponential decay in threshold value.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
